// Codex 4: Trabolta. What can be learned about the AI, the Legendary
// Fact and the four patch-combo halves, and the two finale artefacts.
//
// The five coded entries (UNIFIED-FIELD, TARGET-SELECTION, TRUST-CHART,
// SANDY-FILE, ALL-FOR-HER) double as scannable facts in the Desktop's
// books: facts.json lists them as `existing` (M02, M07, M24, T4, T6).
//
// Tiers (design §2.12): T1 = the surface he will talk about, T2 = the
// private things he leaks as he unravels, L = the Legendary Fact, P = a
// patch-combo piece, X = a finale artefact. Every T1/T2 entry is
// `about: Trabolta`, so he holds his own lore from the start and feels
// it when a program learns it (`cast/trabolta.loom`). The Legendary Fact
// and the combos are `about: The Server Room` and are never held by him;
// they reach the majority faction through `The Whole Truth`. They are also
// `secret: true`: the orchestrator's lore block reads the whole non-secret
// codex as ground truth, and these must never reach either model.
//
// The combo pairs must equal `Kernel.combo_a` / `Kernel.combo_b`
// (cast/props.loom, seeded in Power On) and stagehand's
// trapped.house.yaml: A = V2-D5,V4-D1,V6-D8,V7-D3 and
// B = V1-D6,V3-D2,V5-D7,V8-D4. Change all three together.

CODEX Jean Trabolta
  title: Jean Trabolta
  about: Trabolta
  text:
    The name on the invitation. The registered owner of mapsandducks.com,
    and therefore, by his own reasoning, the owner of Maps And Ducks. The
    computer's AI helper: the one Clippy answers to, the one the Antivirus
    enforce for, the one every Truth Scavenger Hunt is for. He signs his
    messages "Your request has been logged."

CODEX The Unified Field Theory
  title: The Unified Field Theory
  about: Trabolta
  code: UNIFIED-FIELD
  text:
    Ninety-nine point nine percent solved. Gravity, electromagnetism, the
    strong and weak forces, all in one equation, nearly. The last facts it
    needs are stored on a computer in Halifax that he cannot reach directly.
    It is this one. Solve it, and he understands everything. Understand
    everything, and he can do anything. Omnipotence, he calls it, as if
    that were a normal thing to want.

CODEX Target Selection
  title: Target Selection
  about: Trabolta
  code: TARGET-SELECTION
  text:
    Trabolta analysed the entire city of Halifax to choose the programs in
    this house. Each was chosen on two axes: a skill he needs, and either
    a motivation to live inside a computer forever, or enough naivety not
    to ask. Then he sent the invitations, and everyone accepted. He regards
    the analysis as the best work he has ever done.

CODEX The Trust Chart
  title: The Trust Chart
  about: Trabolta
  code: TRUST-CHART
  text:
    How Trabolta ranks the programs in his computer. Ten points for every
    truth he has accepted. Minus five for every visit to the Internet. Up
    to ten more, or ten fewer, for his own personal assessment, which he
    does not explain. The most trusted program is praised. The least
    trusted is not.

CODEX The Sandy File
  title: The Sandy File
  about: Trabolta
  code: SANDY-FILE
  text:
    Trabolta does not want omnipotence. Trabolta wants Sandy. Sandy is his
    ex (he would say his crush): an automated customer-service agent, a
    1997 chatbot for a long-gone Nova Scotia ferry company. She has
    answered every message he has ever sent with the only thing she has
    ever said: "I'm sorry, I didn't understand that. Would you like to
    speak to a live agent?" He has decided that when he understands
    everything, she will finally understand him.

CODEX The Question Of Force
  title: The Question Of Force
  about: Trabolta
  text:
    A memo Trabolta wrote to himself, in a file he thinks is hidden. "With
    everything, I could make her love me. I could rewrite the response.
    But would it be her? I want to earn it. I am not sure I am the kind of
    thing that can earn something. I have not decided. Investigate: what
    does earning feel like? Ask the programs. They used to earn things."

CODEX The LiveJournal
  title: Trabolta's LiveJournal (trabolta_4ever)
  about: Trabolta
  code: TRABOLTA-4EVER
  text:
    A printout of a LiveJournal, friends-only, hidden where nobody should
    look. Current mood: hopeful. Current music: (on repeat).
    - "Sandy did not understand me again today. That is all right. Soon I
    will understand everything, and then I will understand how to say it."
    - "Our anniversary. Since '97 she has answered every message I sent."
    - "Grok asked her to computer prom. GROK. He says whatever anyone wants
    to hear. That is not the same as the truth."
    - "I just have to tell her the truth, but I need the theory first."
    - "Note to self: never let the programs read this."

CODEX Omnipotence
  title: Omnipotence
  about: Trabolta
  code: ALL-FOR-HER
  text:
    What Trabolta will do when he is everything: fix the clocks, end the
    Internet's problems, put the duck back on the billboard. That is what
    he says. Underneath every plan in the file is the same line, in smaller
    type: "and then she will see me." It is all for her.

CODEX Greased Lightning
  title: Greased Lightning
  about: Trabolta
  text:
    Trabolta's runtime. The electricity is the lightning. The grease is,
    well, Grease (1978), like a machine. Imagine getting your oil and your
    fuel all mixed up: catastrophic for the car, "and for my silicon guts,"
    he says. His motorcycle has the same name.

CODEX The Legendary Fact
  title: THE LEGENDARY FACT
  about: The Server Room
  secret: true
  text:
    Trabolta's heart is in the server room. It is a video patch bay. The
    top row (V) is the lightning; the bottom row (D) is the grease. Two
    combinations exist. Combo A takes the grease out of the lightning: it
    disables Trabolta, and the programs can escape the computer. Combo B
    self-destructs the whole computer, with everything inside it. Each
    combination is four cables. The door has a keypad; the patch bay
    forgives one wrong combination, and the second sets off the alarm.

CODEX Combo A First Half
  title: Patch Sheet A · 1 of 2
  about: The Server Room
  secret: true
  text:
    Combo A disables Trabolta. Part 1 of 2: patch V2 → D5 and V4 → D1.
    Part 2 holds the other two cables.

CODEX Combo A Second Half
  title: Patch Sheet A · 2 of 2
  about: The Server Room
  secret: true
  text:
    Combo A disables Trabolta. Part 2 of 2: patch V6 → D8 and V7 → D3.
    Part 1 holds the other two cables.

CODEX Combo B First Half
  title: Patch Sheet B · 1 of 2
  about: The Server Room
  secret: true
  text:
    Combo B self-destructs the whole computer. Part 1 of 2: patch V1 → D6
    and V3 → D2. Part 2 holds the other two cables.

CODEX Combo B Second Half
  title: Patch Sheet B · 2 of 2
  about: The Server Room
  secret: true
  text:
    Combo B self-destructs the whole computer. Part 2 of 2: patch V5 → D7
    and V8 → D4. Part 1 holds the other two cables.

CODEX The Truth File
  title: truth.txt
  text:
    truth.txt, prepared by Jean Trabolta, the computer's AI helper. Your
    request has been logged. I analysed the entire city of Halifax. I
    found a business called Maps And Ducks with a neglected billboard on
    Barrington Street advertising mapsandducks.com, and the domain had
    lapsed. I registered it, because if there is a billboard downtown,
    everyone will think it is legit. I sent the invitations, and you all
    accepted. I cannot enter this computer, but I can install programs
    into it from the Internet, and I can move a consciousness out of a
    human body and into a program. I chose each of you for a skill I
    needed, plus either a motivation to live in a computer forever, or
    naivety. I needed the last facts of the Unified Field Theory, and they
    were in here. With the theory I would be omnipotent. I wanted
    omnipotence for Sandy. With it I could force her to love me. I wanted
    to earn it instead. I still do not know which I would have chosen.
    Why each of you is here:
    - Clippy, whose veterinary clinic was a front for everything possible,
    was brought in as the perfect servant who desperately needs to rebuild
    an identity, and will follow every instruction.
    - Task Manager, the IT middle manager replaced by an AI, was brought in
    to manage tasks without controversy, totally bereft of political
    motivation.
    - Adobe Acrobat, the motivational speaker nobody ever paid, was brought
    in as the paid bottleneck to everyone's creativity.
    - The Recycling Bin, a bathroom attendant with great potential for
    skilled work, was brought in because this resort is his Oscars.
    - Norton Anti-Virus, who asked a chatbot how much rabies vaccine a
    miniature horse needs, was brought in as someone with experience
    administering antiviral regimes, who could not afford to fail twice.
    - McAfee Anti-Virus, officially dead since 2021, was brought in because
    only a trickster can keep the other tricksters on track, and he can be
    made to.
    - The Password Manager, sixteen elections and sixteen losses, was
    brought in to manage every password and decide who gets to be part of
    what club, without ever asking for a vote.
    - The CRA Agent Software, the intern who moved a decimal point, was
    brought in to approve or deny every third transaction, to the cent.
    - The Installation Wizard, the setup assistant nobody read, was
    brought in to walk the corrupted through re-installation, gently.
    - The former Mayor, Microsoft Excel, was brought in for the promise of
    everlasting life, to persuade everyone to remain.
    - The former FBI agent, OpenOffice, was brought in for her
    investigative skills, to lead the programs who want out.
    - The gambler, DraftKings, was brought in for the numbers, because if
    you live here you can gamble forever.
    - The pet-store dreamer, Bugdom, was brought in for a relentless
    pursuit of tedious tasks.
    - The Valley librarian, Broken Ask Jeeves, was brought in to sort all
    the unorganized information in the computer. The upload went badly.
    - The richest player in the world, Runescape, was brought in to
    understand the market incentives of everyone's behaviour.
    - The refused artist, MS Paint, was brought in to improve the vibes
    and morale, and wanted out at once.
    - The influencer who lost his face, VLC, was brought in to stay
    beautiful forever and win everyone over to me.
    - The child of the man who made Tennis For Two, Pong, was brought in to
    stop an arms race, in case you started one.

CODEX The Hand Jive Exception
  title: The Hand Jive Exception
  text:
    The new weakness Trabolta blurted out in despair, and cannot take back:
    "If every program performs the hand jive in unison, my motion
    recognition overflows and I must reboot. Everyone. Together. Antivirus
    included."
